---
import Home from '../../index.astro';

/*
 * The project-shaped entry page — which is src/pages/index.astro, rendered
 * with its other `shape`.
 *
 * This file used to be a second copy of the whole page, with a header comment
 * claiming it was "what a `project` preset init keeps at /". It was not:
 * init swapped one hero import in index.astro and deleted this directory, so
 * `--preset project` produced a project hero above a personal body. Now there
 * is one page carrying both shapes, marked up with ▼ PRESET:… ▼ fences, and
 * this route exists only to give the demo switcher a second URL to point at.
 *
 * An .astro page is an ordinary component, so importing it is all it takes.
 * Everything a visitor sees here — the hero, the sections, the styles — is in
 * index.astro; nothing is duplicated, and nothing can drift.
 *
 * Deleted by `npm run init` along with the switcher: the `demo` feature owns
 * src/pages/demo/, and once a preset is chosen there is only one shape left.
 */
---

<Home shape="project" />
